Hello Adventurers!

We’ve just released the hotfix 2.3.4, which is fixing all achievements with repetitive activities from Spirits of Amazonia expansions 1-3.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/32791864/bcc715f2a8c1a31ae6049075ae16c326edb64f07.png
The complete list of fixed achievements is as follows:

 Babysitter (Return 9 kids to safety);
 Molineria-man (Heal a Tribe member); 
 Rest in peace (Burn 10 Tribe Members’ corpses);
 Cleaning volunteer (Burn 10 Toxic Waste Piles);
 Fishing in troubled water (Help 5 Tribe Fishermen);
 Handyman (Rebuild 10 Tribe Totems);
 Cage opener (Free 9 Tribe Women).

We know that there might be issues with triggering achievements from a loaded game in which a quest has already been finished - we strongly suggest loading the game save from the Main Menu, not the Pause menu. Also, we are aware that there are still issues with the achievements gained in the co-op mode, and with the “That’s the spirit!” achievement (Complete all Spirits of Amazonia achievements) -  we’re currently working on a fix to them as well. 

If you happen to stumble upon an issue with triggering achievements, we would be really thankful for letting us know here in the comments, or at support@creepyjar.com.

Stay tuned as we prepare new updates,

Creepy Jar Team
